# Project Map: App Server Dashboard Performance Truth

Status: active
Type: project-map
Updated: 2026-08-30

## Purpose

Make the hosted App Server fleet screen accurately distinguish readiness, routing opportunities,
real executions, reliability, and execution cost so an operator can size the integration without
mistaking selections or control events for completed work.

## Desired Outcome

For every reporting instance, the dashboard shows current App Server readiness and clearly
bounded 24-hour, 7-day, and 30-day execution summaries sourced from the real execution ledger,
with 7 days as the useful default. The summary separates
planning, verification, and CAMP work; distinguishes completed, failed, interrupted, and GUI
fallback outcomes; and exposes enough latency, token, and cache evidence to judge operational
overhead without claiming billing cost or unsupported GUI comparisons.

## First Useful Boundary

- Derive availability from current runtime readiness rather than selection count.
- Aggregate real top-level App Server executions while excluding preference, selection, and
  recovery-control events from attempt counts.
- Report selectable exact bounded windows, last execution, role and outcome counts, duration percentiles, token
  totals/per-run values, cache ratio, and weighted-usage proxy.
- Keep CAMP success stricter than protocol completion by using verified journal state where
  available and preserving unknown historical evidence honestly.
- Extend the privacy allowlist and hosted read model without transmitting prompts, responses,
  paths, campaign names, raw diagnostics, credentials, or secrets.
- Present a compact fleet summary and instance table with browser-local timestamps, then qualify
  the candidate on the combined live Work2 target.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Local metric truth | One bounded aggregate over readiness, execution telemetry, and fallbacks | existing local ledgers |
| Report contract | Strict schema extension for content-free performance metrics | local metric truth |
| Hosted read model | Persist and ingest the new per-instance aggregate | report contract |
| Operator screen | Scannable readiness, reliability, and sizing presentation | hosted read model |
| Qualification | Privacy, aggregation, migration, rendering, browser, and target evidence | complete vertical slice |

## Evidence Gates

1. `G1-REAL-EXECUTION-TRUTH`: attempts and outcomes come from actual top-level executions, not
   selections, preferences, or recovery controls, with explicit handling of historical unknowns.
2. `G2-READINESS-AND-WINDOW-TRUTH`: readiness, observation time, report freshness, execution
   window, and browser-local last-execution time are visible and semantically distinct.
3. `G3-PERFORMANCE-SIZING`: role breakdown, success/interruption/fallback posture, duration
   percentiles, token intensity, cache ratio, and weighted usage proxy are bounded and correctly
   labelled.
4. `G4-PRIVACY-AND-WORK2`: strict contract rejection, focused tests, live deployment, browser
   checks, release-cohort registration, checkpoint/rebuild proof, and strict Doctor pass.

## Constraints

- Local Tool Shed state remains authoritative and hosted reporting remains advisory.
- Unknown or unclassified historical evidence stays unknown; it is never guessed into operator or
  qualification workload.
- Weighted usage is a relative proxy, not currency, billing, or ChatGPT allowance consumption.
- The report remains bounded and content-free.

## Non-Goals

- Long-term trend storage, charts, rankings, or an arbitrary analytics API.
- Fabricated GUI baselines, savings claims, or cost estimates.
- Changing App Server routing, qualification, permissions, or provider policy.

